<figure class="security-figure" aria-labelledby="architecture-caption">
  <div class="security-boundaries">
    <div class="security-zone security-zone--device">
      <div class="security-zone-heading">
        <span class="security-eyebrow">Client boundary</span>
        <h3>Your device</h3>
        <p>Keys are opened and content is decrypted here.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="security-local-flow" role="list">
        <li>
          <span class="security-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div>
            <h4>Unlock the local keyring</h4>
            <p>A host wrapping key protects the account root. A PIN can add another layer.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="security-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>
            <h4>Derive separate local keys</h4>
            <p>Dedicated keys for the database, blob store, and identity persistence.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="security-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div>
            <h4>Keep local storage encrypted</h4>
            <p>The app reads and writes through encrypted database and blob storage.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="security-zone-note">Plaintext is available to the unlocked app.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="security-sync-bridge">
      <span>Encrypted<br />sync</span>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 80 32" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M4 10h70m-7-6 7 6-7 6M76 23H6m7-6-7 6 7 6" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="security-zone security-zone--service">
      <div class="security-zone-heading">
        <span class="security-eyebrow">Service boundary</span>
        <h3>Sync &amp; storage</h3>
        <p>The API stores and delivers encrypted records.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="security-service-records">
        <div>
          <dt>Encrypted payloads</dt>
          <dd>Document updates, files, and encrypted metadata.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Wrapped keys</dt>
          <dd>Encrypted key envelopes that authorized clients can open.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Signed access records</dt>
          <dd>Verifiable policies, grants, and content-write commitments.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="security-zone-note">No plaintext content keys held by the service.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="architecture-caption">
    <span class="security-figure-label">Figure 01</span>{" "}
    Local storage and remote content encryption use separate key layers.
    Sync exchanges encrypted records and access metadata, not the local database.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
